From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] btmgmt: use rl_clear_message to clear the readline message

Avoid passing an argument to rl_message, whose declaration in the target
readline headers is an old-style unspecified-arguments prototype.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/btmgmt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/btmgmt.c b/tools/btmgmt.c
--- a/tools/btmgmt.c
+++ b/tools/btmgmt.c
@@ -4879,6 +4879,6 @@
 		io_destroy(input);
 
-		rl_message("");
+		rl_clear_message();
 		rl_callback_handler_remove();
 	}
 
